== Effects ==
* +1 [[damage]].
* Adds a chance to shoot [[fear|fear tears]], causing enemies to run away from Isaac.

== Notes ==
* {{dlc+|r+}} This item has a 1% chance to drop when defeating {{e|Dark One}}.{{dlc-}}
* Fear tear effect depends on the [[luck]] stat, and the formula used to determine the chance is: <math>\frac1 { 3 - \left \lfloor \mathit{Luck} * 0.1 \right \rfloor}</math>
** At base luck (0), the chance is 33.33%, maxing out at 100% at 20 luck.
** This makes Dark Matter significantly better at inflicting fear than {{i|Abaddon}} or {{i|Mom's Perfume}}.
* {{dlc+|r+}} Dark Matter's quality is treated as 2 for the purposes of {{I|Bag of Crafting}}.{{dlc-}}

== Synergies ==
* {{i|Brimstone}}: Laser applies fear to enemies more consistently due to its tick rate.
* {{i|Compound Fracture}}/{{i|Cricket's Body}}/{{i|The Parasite}}: Chance for tears and split tears to cause fear. If the main tear causes fear, the split tears cause fear too.

== Interactions ==
* {{i|Haemolacria}}: Tear appearance stays the same; only the main tear can cause fear.
* {{i|Lachryphagy}}: If a fear tear is fed, all burst tears cause fear. If a normal tear is fed, the burst tears cannot cause fear.
* {{i|The Ludovico Technique}}: Tear occasionally changes appearance to Dark Matter tears and causes fear.

